Aim

To create billing alerts in Oracle Cloud for monitoring cloud spending and budget limits.

Requirements
Oracle Cloud Account
Internet Connection
Email ID
Step 1: Login to Oracle Cloud

Open:

Oracle Cloud Console

Enter:

Username
Password

Click:

Sign In

Step 2: Open Billing Section

Click:

☰ Menu (Top Left)

Go to:

Billing & Cost Management
→ Budgets

If not visible:
Use search bar and type:

Budgets

Step 3: Create Budget

Click:

Create Budget

Step 4: Enter Budget Details

Fill the fields:

Field	Value
Name	MonthlyBudget
Compartment	Root Compartment
Budget Amount	1000 INR

Select:

Monthly Budget Reset

Step 5: Add Alert Rule

Scroll down to:

Alert Rules

Click:

Add Alert Rule

Step 6: Configure Alert Percentage

Enter:

Threshold	Meaning
50	Alert at 50% usage
80	Alert at 80% usage
100	Alert at full budget

You can add multiple alerts.

Step 7: Add Email Notification

Under:

Recipients

Enter:

Your Email Address

Example:

abc@gmail.com
Step 8: Save Budget

Click:

Create Budget

Budget alert configuration is completed.

Step 9: Verify Email

Check your email inbox.

Oracle may send:

Budget Notification Confirmation

Verify if needed.

Step 10: View Budget Dashboard

Now you can see:

Current Spending
Budget Amount
Forecast Cost
Alert Rules

inside:

Billing Dashboard

Step 11: Test Billing Alert

If your cloud usage increases:

Oracle automatically sends email alerts.

Example:

50% budget reached
80% budget reached
Step 12: Monitor Spending

Go regularly to:

Billing & Cost Management
→ Cost Analysis

You can monitor:

Daily spending
Monthly spending
Service-wise spending
Implementation & Result

Successfully:

Created monthly budget
Configured billing thresholds
Added email notifications
Enabled budget monitoring

Billing alerts were configured successfully.
